# DOS kernel runtime state (regenerated on every tool call). ANCHORED on purpose
# (#5933): an unanchored `.dos/` matches at every depth, so a state root nested
# inside the tree is invisible to `git status`, returns 0 from `git ls-files`,
# and is excluded from `ls-files --others --exclude-standard` by construction —
# while the positional walk still resolves the lease journal there and reports
# every lane free. The toplevel's own root stays ignored; a nested one is now a
# visible untracked directory, which is the only cheap way to notice it.
/.dos/

# Slack control bridge runtime state (regenerated on each control operation)
fak/.slack_control_*

# Compiled build artifacts (regenerable from source via `go build`)
*.exe

# Cross-platform node-benchmark build dir (tools/fak_node_bench.sh; binaries have no
# .exe extension on macOS/Linux). (Node-bench result outputs are ignored below per the
# operator-requested regenerable-output rule.)
fak/.benchbin/

# Built fak binary dropped by run_local_model.sh / dogfood-claude.sh (regenerable via
# `go build ./cmd/fak`). The scripts are tracked; the binary they build is not.
tools/.bin/

# Python bytecode cache (created when tools/*.py import each other)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Regenerable operator snapshots written by the /plan-audit skill (re-run anytime)
docs/_audits/

# Raw session-status / working-note `.txt` drops under docs/benchmarks are transient
# operator notes (a session's live blockers, internal paths, bring-up state) — NOT the
# curated public results docs, which are ALL `.md`. By default these belong in the
# private notes repo (../fak-private), the same as a session's brainstorm/audit notes.
# Ignoring the `.txt` class here makes that the default: a stray status note can never be
# `git add`-ed into this public tree by accident (same private-by-default guard pattern
# as the bench-node run dirs further below). Curated `.md` benchmark docs stay tracked.
docs/benchmarks/*.txt

# Local rendered exports; source markdown is tracked.
docs/explainers/kv-cache-agentic-context.html
docs/explainers/kv-cache-agentic-context.pdf

# Regenerable run-output drops that otherwise re-leak into `git status` every session
# on the shared trunk (a trajectory-audit finding): process stdout/stderr redirects at
# the repo root, the empty experiments run-scaffold, and the industry-scorecard cadence
# output (written by tools/industry_freshness_cadence.py). The SCRIPTS are tracked; the
# state they emit is not — same private-by-default guard as the bench-node run dirs below.
# Root-level *_out.txt / *_err.txt are shell stdout/stderr redirects from ad-hoc
# `fak serve`/`scout`/probe runs (serve_*, scout_*, …); ignore the class so a new probe
# name never re-leaks. Tracked .txt elsewhere is unaffected (these are anchored to root).
/*_out.txt
/*_err.txt
experiments/registry.jsonl
docs/industry-scorecard/cadence-output/

# Fleet session/watchdog runtime state — machine-local generated snapshots, logs and
# PID/lease tracking (timestamps, live PIDs, account throttle windows). Regenerated on
# every supervisor/resume-watchdog tick; the SCRIPTS under tools/ are tracked, the state
# they write is not.
tools/_registry/
tools/_watchdog/
tools/_walltime.*

# Local live-dogfood scratch state: try-it PID files, logs, and one-off console proof
# artifacts. Regenerated per operator session.
.dogfood/
# Per-session agent scratch dirs (issue-comment drafts, scratch src/test, index dumps).
.scratch/
.cscratch/
# Per-session `go build -overlay` scratch: the overlay JSON specs (ov_build.json,
# overlay*.json) plus the substitute/emptied `.go` sources they swap in to hide a peer's
# untracked WIP from a compile-check (the `fak buildcheck` overlay mechanism; AGENTS.md).
# Regenerated per probe run, never a build input to the tracked tree — private-by-default
# so a probe copy of guard.go/a test can never be `git add`-ed onto the shared trunk.
.probe/

# Scratch / temp leaks that occasionally land in the tree when a tool writes to a relative
# path instead of an absolute temp dir (e.g. a flattened C...scratchpad...json at the repo
# root, or a *tmp working dir). Private-by-default so they can never be `git add`-ed; the
# FILE_ADMISSION gate is the commit-time backstop for anything that slips past these globs.
*scratchpad*
# ...but a tracked note ABOUT the scratchpad concept is legitimate, not a leak.
!docs/notes/*SCRATCHPAD*
# One-off `*_scratch.json` dumps a tool writes to the repo root (e.g.
# ready_leaves_scratch.json) — per-session throwaway, never a build input.
*_scratch.json
# Dispatch/routing scratch dumps the issue-dispatch tooling writes to the repo
# root (leaves2.json, ready_tmp.json, router_ready.json, lanes_ready.json,
# router_tmp.json, cp_out.json/cp_scratch*, after.json, and the dispatch-loop
# tick dumps _dloop_router.json/_dloop_tick*.json). Per-session throwaway,
# never a build input — but tree-scan governance tests (branchrole ref-audit,
# pythongate, the tier/classification suites) walk the whole tree and red on a
# stray `origin/main` string or a stored issue title inside them. Scope to the
# root so a real tracked `*_ready.json` in a package (there are none today) is
# never hidden.
/*_tmp.json
/*_ready.json
/leaves*.json
/lanes_ready.json
/cp_out.json
/cp_scratch*.json
/after.json
/_dloop_*.json
# router_p0p1.json and future priority-band router dumps (the issue-lane router's
# `fleet-issue-lane-router/1` verdict report, a generated routing snapshot). The
# router_ready/router_tmp dumps are already caught by /*_ready.json and /*_tmp.json
# above; this generalizes the family so a p0p1/p2-band dump can't slip through.
# Root-scoped; no tracked router_*.json exists.
/router_*.json
# Root-level stderr redirect dumps (`fak ... 2> route.err.txt`) — per-session
# throwaway, often empty. Scoped to the root so a tracked `*.err.txt` fixture in a
# package (e.g. experiments/agent-live/*.err.txt) is never hidden.
/*.err.txt
**/rmverifytmp/
**/*verifytmp/

# Regen / run-artifact leaks that accumulate in the shared dogfood tree. None of these are
# inputs to a build — they are per-session scratch (.regen-scratch/ holds regenerated copies
# of the top-level docs), DOS run telemetry (dos.runs/*.json), a one-off lane-isolation
# helper, transient .isoprobe-<n>/ isolation-probe checkouts (throwaway source copies a
# lane-isolation probe drops at the repo root), or the .run.{err,out,log} sidecars that
# `fak sweep` already classifies as junk.
.regen-scratch/
.isoprobe-*/
dos.runs/
/.split_reconstruct.py
*.run.err
*.run.out
*.run.log

# --- Artifact-shaped leaks a tool/process drops into the working tree. Private-by-default so
# they can never be `git add`-ed and never dirty `git status`. Root-scoped where the name is
# generic; family-shaped so a NEW generator's raw output is contained by default. The
# FILE_ADMISSION commit gate stays the backstop for anything that slips past these globs. ---

# Build-verification extraction dirs: a build-probe that untars `git archive HEAD` into a
# repo-root dir instead of an os.MkdirTemp scratch — the same throwaway-source-copy family as
# .isoprobe-*/ above. The canonical .head_build_check/ is ignored explicitly further below (with
# its windowgate double-count rationale); this family glob contains any variant that does not.
/*_build_check/

# Per-session verify/probe scratch dirs (extends .scratch/ .cscratch/): .scratch-q4k-verify/,
# .scratch_q4k_70/ and friends. Root-scoped so a tracked .scratch* fixture is never hidden.
/.scratch*/

# Spam/evidence report dir a tool drops beside the repo. Its *.local.json payloads are already
# ignored by the `.local` convention above; the dir rule also contains any non-.local artifact.
/.spam-report/

# Ad-hoc redirect spills at the repo root (`fak ... > out.json 2> err.log`). Root-scoped so a
# tracked out*.json / err*.log fixture in a package is never hidden (extends /*.err.txt above).
/out*.json
/err*.log

# Git's own 3-way-merge scratch copies (`git merge-file` / a rename-conflict checkout drops
# `.merge_file_XXXXXX` in the working tree). Always throwaway, never a build input. Root-scoped.
/.merge_file_*

# One-off session runner scripts a dispatch/report loop writes to the repo root
# (`.run-<seed>.sh`, an `exec bash scripts/...` wrapper pointed at /tmp state). Per-session
# throwaway — same family as the *.run.log spills above.
/.run-*.sh

# gh-issue-list JSON dumps a triage query redirects to the repo root (`gh issue list --json ... > perf.json`).
# Root-scoped so a tracked perf.json fixture in a package is never hidden.
/perf.json

# Throwaway temp generator / run dirs at the repo root: tmpgenfeeds/ (a one-off `package main`
# feed generator), fleet-runs/ (nightrun poll/watch logs), workfak/ (a nested dispatch scratch
# copy). Distinctive-prefix globs — no tracked dir matches (a bare /tmp*/ could catch a future
# /tmpl/, so the tmp family is scoped to the tmpgen* generator prefix).
/tmpgen*/
/fleet-runs/
/workfak/

