# Regenerable benchmark outputs — ignored per operator request (2026-06-17) to keep
# `git status` quiet. NOTE: this REVERSES the repo's prior convention of tracking these
# (model-baseline/ and fleet/eraser/ already have committed csv/json; fleet-nodes/ was
# documented as tracked above). Already-committed files under these paths stay tracked
# unless deliberately removed, so only NEW outputs are hidden by these rules.
fak/experiments/fleet-nodes/
fak/experiments/dgx/
experiments/dgx/
# Raw per-machine benchmark run drops (experiments/benchmark/runs/by-machine/
# <machine>/<UTC>-<label>/) are PRIVATE-BY-DEFAULT. They are regenerable harness
# output, and they routinely carry infrastructure tells that must never reach the
# public tree: cloud instance names + zones and credential file paths in the fleet
# witness.json drops, VM hostnames and accelerator SKUs in the gcp result/manifest
# drops, private multi-GPU topology in the a100/dgx captures, and local box paths /
# core counts elsewhere. Historically ONLY machine_id=dgx* was ignored (the
# PRIVATE-ONLY GPU server lab, registered by tools/bench_slack.py) — too narrow:
# every other machine's drops accumulated in the public tree until 133 files had
# landed. Ignoring the whole tree makes a run registered in ANY clone private by
# default and never `git add`-able by accident.
#
# This does NOT lose run history. The durable public record is the tracked aggregate
# experiments/benchmark/catalog.json: tools/bench_catalog.py builds it by UNION
# (merge, not scan-and-replace) and validate treats an absent run dir as a warning,
# precisely so the artifacts can be gitignored on a driver/agent-host clone.
# `fak bench-runs list/summary/table/best` read the catalog and are unaffected; only
# `show` degrades to catalog-entry-only output.
#
# Already-committed evidence artifacts stay tracked — gitignore is inert for tracked
# paths — so the BENCHMARK-AUTHORITY.md anchors (gpu-server-sglang serving-parity,
# node-macos-a q4k score.json) and the doc-cited run dirs keep resolving in a public
# clone. To PUBLISH a new run artifact, scrub it first (tools/scrub_public_copy.py)
# and then promote it deliberately with `git add -f <path>`; a bare `git add` can no
# longer do it silently. Keep both layouts: the private superrepo nests the module
# under fak/, while this public checkout is root-hoisted.
fak/experiments/benchmark/runs/by-machine/
experiments/benchmark/runs/by-machine/
fak/experiments/benchmarks/tb4-*/
experiments/benchmarks/tb4-*/
# Atomic-write temp sibling of the tracked experiments/benchmark/catalog.json: the
# catalog writer renders to catalog.tmp then renames over catalog.json, and a crashed
# or racing write leaves the .tmp behind. Regenerable, never source. Scoped to the dir
# so a real tracked *.tmp elsewhere is untouched (none exist under benchmark today).
/experiments/benchmark/*.tmp
# `fak nightrun --apply` captures each task's raw stdout under experiments/nightrun/<box>/.
# Those per-box dirs are LOCAL evidence only: regenerable, low-signal (mostly failure logs),
# and one carries a raw os.Hostname() box dir (pre-#970) that must never reach the public tree.
# The live durable record is now .fak/nightrun/collected.jsonl (the gitignored runtime
# root, #3209); the tracked docs/nightrun/collected.jsonl is a periodic publication
# snapshot of it, not the live writer target. The operator overlay
# experiments/nightrun/backlog.json stays tracked (a shareable input, not an artifact).
# docs/nightrun/cache-value.jsonl is a per-run scratch sibling of collected.jsonl —
# regenerated each nightrun, not the durable ledger, so it stays out of the tree.
fak/experiments/nightrun/*/
experiments/nightrun/*/
docs/nightrun/cache-value.jsonl
# Legacy pre-86dbfe7fa guard processes wrote per-session step-advice stamps into
# tracked docs. New guards write beside .fak/trajctl.jsonl; keep old still-running
# processes and restored sessions from re-dirtying the shared tree (#4276).
docs/nightrun/stepadvice-*.json
# Do NOT blanket-ignore docs/nightrun: the dir holds curated, TRACKED publication
# snapshots (README.md, the *.md plans, collected.jsonl). A whole-dir `/docs/nightrun`
# rule neither untracks them (gitignore is inert for already-tracked paths) nor should
# hide them; it only masks a future stray. Scope ignores to the regenerable siblings
# above, and reverse a stray re-add with `git rm --cached`. History: #4276 git-rm'd the
# legacy stamps and added the rule above; commit e041fdd42 (a broad `git add`) re-added
# all 192 despite the rule — the README's "must never return to the index" invariant.
# Shadow nightrun tree: telemetry writers were CWD-relative, so a guard/serve run — most
# visibly `go test ./cmd/fak` (cwd=cmd/fak) — forked docs/nightrun UNDER cmd/fak and left
# it tracked-but-perpetually-dirty. The writers now anchor to the repo root
# (cmd/fak/nightrun_ledger_path.go) so this is no longer created; ignore it as
# defense-in-depth so a future stray CWD-relative write can never be re-added. `docs/`
# under cmd/fak is never a legit tracked artifact (docs/ is a repo-root concept).
cmd/fak/docs/
# Same CWD-relative-writer bug class as cmd/fak/docs/ above: a bench/catalog writer run
# with cwd=cmd/fak (e.g. `go test ./cmd/fak`) forks the repo-root experiments/ tree
# UNDER cmd/fak, leaving an empty experiments/benchmark/runs/by-machine/ shadow that
# perpetually dirties `git status`. experiments/ is a repo-root concept — never a legit
# tracked artifact under cmd/fak — so ignore it as defense-in-depth against a stray
# CWD-relative write, exactly as with cmd/fak/docs/.
cmd/fak/experiments/
# DGX Slack control-bridge source is PRIVATE-ONLY. Its home is the private repo
# fak-private (tools/dgxbridge/); fleet is the sunset archive. tools/check_committed_files.py
# already REFUSES any cmd|internal/*dgx*/ path at commit (this is exactly how cmd/dgxbridge +
# internal/dgxbridge leaked once); these ignore rules also keep a stray working copy out of
# `git status` so an auto-ship never tries to add it. Un-prefixed to match this repo's
# module-at-root layout — the fak/-prefixed rules above are inert in a public clone.
cmd/*dgx*/
internal/*dgx*/
cmd/slackgc/
