# --- merged from former fak/.gitignore (module at root now) ---
# build output — the compiled binary at the module root ONLY. This MUST stay
# anchored (`/fak`): a bare `fak` also matches the `cmd/fak/` SOURCE directory,
# which silently un-tracked the CLI entrypoint (`cmd/fak/main.go`) before v0.2.
/fak
fak.exe
*.exe
# Windows leaves a `<name>.exe~` when `go build -o` can't atomically replace a
# binary that is still mapped (e.g. a running `fak serve`). Regenerable scratch.
*.exe~
# Self-update / hot-swap binary asides beside the repo-root fak.exe. `*.exe` above hides
# fak.exe itself but NOT the rename-aside files the Windows atomic swap must leave next to it
# (a mapped .exe can't be overwritten in place): fak.exe.old / fak.exe.old.<pid>.<i> swap-asides
# (internal/selfinstall/runner.go — a real host accumulated 211 of these, ~9 GB), the fak.exe.new
# build-temp left on a vet/smoke gate-failure return (selfinstall.go), and manual
# fak.exe.bak-<ts> / fak.exe.old-<sha> backups. These MUST sit next to the binary, so containment
# (not relocation) is the fix; root-scoped /fak.exe.* catches every suffix without hiding fak.exe.
/fak.exe.*

# Same containment rule on the POSIX side: when the installed binary is the in-checkout
# /fak, internal/selfinstall leaves its transaction state beside it — the verified
# rollback slot fak.self-update-prior (launchstate.go) and the live install-identity
# fak.self-update-identity.json (identity.go IdentityStatePath). Both are runtime state
# owned by selfinstall, NOT repo output: the identity json is what a later
# `fak self-update` reads to verify/roll back, so never delete or relocate it; root-scoped
# /fak.self-update-* catches every suffix without hiding /fak.
/fak.self-update-*

# transient stderr captured by the dogfood launchers (committed evidence is the
# probe JSON next to it, not the log)
