# Regenerable turn-tax + kvmmu witness reports. WRITTEN BY TESTS, not curated:
# internal/turnbench/stochastic_test.go writes experiments/turn-tax/turntax-{stochastic,
# breakeven}.json (and reads them back as its own fixtures — "a new file" per the test),
# and internal/kvmmu/kvmmu_test.go drops a kvmmu-report.json. Same regenerable-bench-output
# class as /turntax-report.json above; ignore the regenerable *.json so re-running the
# suite (any seed bump, any clone) leaves git status quiet. The .go SOURCES stay tracked.
# Glob the .json class only (NOT the directory): a dir-slash ignore can't be re-included
# from, but curated artifacts here — e.g. turntax-breakeven.png, produced by
# tools/turntax_plot.py and CITED by TURN-TAX-RESULTS.md — must stay committable so the
# ship-iff-cited gate (tools/public_evidence_manifest.py --check) can see them in CI.
/experiments/turn-tax/*.json
/experiments/kvmmu/*.json
# ...and re-include the three that a PUBLISHED doc cites by name. The blanket ignore
# above was cutting them out of the public tree while the docs went on pointing at them,
# so ship-iff-cited failed in CI on every run: KV-QUARANTINE-BRIDGE-RESULTS.md even calls
# kvmmu-report.json "committed" twice (its "every number is a go test line or a committed
# ...field" framing, and the witness-table row), which was simply untrue. The quiet-status
# rationale above does not apply to these three: each emitter rewrites its file
# byte-identically (witnessed — hash unchanged across `go test ./internal/kvmmu/ -run
# TestEmitReport` and `go test ./internal/turnbench/`), so they behave like the committed,
# generated hero SVGs rather than like churning bench output. The turn-tax pair embeds
# app_version, so a release bump does dirty them until regenerated — that is the ordinary
# cost of a committed generated artifact, not the per-run churn this block guards against.
!/experiments/turn-tax/turntax-breakeven.json
!/experiments/turn-tax/turntax-stochastic.json
!/experiments/kvmmu/kvmmu-report.json

# --- scrub/adjudication session scratch (node-local; never commit) ----------------
# .adjudicate/ holds one-off diffs + copies of the PRIVATE `fleet` repo's scrub
# tooling (fleet_scrub_public_copy.py / fleet_PUBLIC-SCRUB-POLICY.md / fleet_SUNSET.md),
# which carry the real-secret denylist by reference — the exact content the
# PUBLIC-SCRUB-POLICY leak gate keeps out of this public tree. Never stage it.
/.adjudicate/

# --- credential-shaped stray files (the FILENAME is the secret) -------------------
# A stray shell redirect (e.g. `cmd > "$TOKEN"`) can create a file whose NAME is a
# live-shaped Anthropic OAuth token (sk-ant-oat01-...). The 46-byte content is
# innocuous (a path), but the token-shaped filename would be written into git
# history by any `git add -A`. Never stage it. (Rotate the token + delete the file
# is an operator action — this rule only stops the leak vector.)
sk-ant-*
sk-ant-oat01-*

# --- runtime demo artifact (regenerated on every run) -----------------------------
# cmd/memqdemo writes memqdemo-report.json into its working dir on each run as the
# machine-readable witness of that run; it is a build product, not source. Track the
# code that emits it, not the emission.
memqdemo-report.json

# --- ad-hoc session scratch on the shared trunk (node-local; never commit) --------
# These re-leak into `git status` every session on the shared trunk (the same
# trajectory-audit finding the root *_out.txt / *_err.txt rules above address) and
# carry no durable signal — they are one-off analysis scripts, scorecard JSON dumps,
# and commit-message drops a session writes while working. The TOOLS that emit them
# (tools/code_slop_scorecard.py, `fak commit -F msgfile`, the AEO scorecard) are
# tracked; this transient run state is not. Anchored to the module root where the
# name is generic, so a tracked file of the same name elsewhere is unaffected.
#   scratch_*  : ad-hoc throwaway analysis scripts / JSON a session writes at root
#   /slop*.json: code-slop-scorecard output (regenerable via the tracked scorecard)
#   .aeo_* .aeo-*: agent-experience-optimization scorecard session scratch
#   /_tmp_*    : one-off gate/preview scratch (json/md)
#   /.tmp/     : root session scratch dir (fs dumps, pin-check checkout copies);
#                tree-walking gates (refaudit, scorecards) prune gitignored paths,
#                so an unignored .tmp reddens them with phantom findings
#   /.tmp_overlay/ /.ovl/ : `go test -overlay` gate scratch — the overlay JSON, its
#                stub replacements, and a `head/` git-archive of HEAD for the
#                standalone build proof. Must live in-tree (the OUT_OF_TREE_WRITE
#                guard refuses external writes), so it can't go to the scratchpad;
#                ignore both names so a 100+MB checkout tree never re-leaks into
#                `git status`. Prefer /.tmp_overlay/ (or a /_ovl/ under the /_* root
#                namespace) for new runs rather than minting more dotted names.
#   /*_msg_*.txt: `fak commit` message drops (commit_msg_*, docs_msg_*)
#   /err.txt   : a bare stderr redirect drop
/scratch_*
/slop.json
/slop_*.json
.aeo_*
.aeo-*
/_tmp_*
/.tmp/
/.tmp_overlay/
/.ovl/
/*_msg_*.txt
/err.txt

# --- scratch NAMESPACE (denylist -> allowlist inversion) --------------------------
# Everything above this point NAMES each scratch file reactively, so a session that
# invents a new scratch name always escapes the list until a new rule is chased in. The
# fleet has converged on a '_'-prefix-at-root convention for throwaway drops (_route.err,
# _build.err, _issues.json, _devleaves.json, _censuswitness/, _scratch3057/, ...), so
# ignore that NAMESPACE by default and stop playing whack-a-mole. Redirect deliberate
# scratch into /_scratch/ (already covered by /_* below).
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED ONLY — this is the load-bearing safety property. Tracked '_' paths all
# live NESTED (blog/_*.md, docs/_config.yml, docs/_includes/, tools/**/_*.json,
# visuals/_meta.json), so a bare `**/_*` would silently un-track them. `git ls-files |
# grep '^_'` is empty, which is exactly what makes `/_*` safe at the repo root. To TRACK
# a new root path that starts with '_', re-include it explicitly, e.g. `!/_wanted`.
#
# A no-prefix leak (a bare `err` stderr redirect) can't be caught by a namespace and
# still needs an explicit name; the FILE_ADMISSION commit gate
# (tools/check_committed_files.py) stays the fail-closed backstop for anything a glob misses.
/_*
/err
# Scratch probe programs parked under cmd/ (cmd/_shortfallcheck/, cmd/_stallverify/). Go
# already skips '_'-prefixed dirs from ./... builds; this keeps them out of git too.
cmd/_*

# Trajectory-audit drops written by `fak trajectory audit` carry PRIVATE operator
# telemetry, including per-session token totals and local source paths. Raw machine-local
# dumps must not land in this public tree; committed analysis cites selected numbers.
/audit-sessions.json
/trajectory-audit-*.json
/trajectory-audit-*.md
/.verify1259

# Scratch goal specs (disposable active loop memory; first-class coordination lives in leases, claims, and comments)
/GOAL.md
/GOAL-*.md

