# `.go.scratch` probe files — a test file parked with a .scratch suffix so `go test`
# skips it while a spike is in flight (e.g. anthropic_toolref_probe*_test.go.scratch).
# The suffix already excludes it from the build; this keeps it out of `git status` too.
*.go.scratch

# `.txt.done` / `.commitmsg-*.done` completion markers a loop drops beside its input
# to signal "consumed" — node-local bookkeeping, not source.
*.txt.done

# Scratch worktrees / relay-probe dirs an operator spins up beside the clone for a
# one-off check, then forgets to remove (.dogfood-wt/ carries a throwaway msg.txt,
# .scratch-relaycheck/ a throwaway main.go). Never source.
/.dogfood-wt/
/.scratch-relaycheck/

# HEAD build-check scratch tree — a full git-archive checkout of HEAD dropped beside the
# clone by the prepush/blind-base build probe so it can `go build` committed-only source.
# Regenerable, 100+MB, and (crucially) tree-walking governance gates like windowgate's
# TestTrackedTreeHasNoPopups would otherwise scan the mirrored copy and double-count every
# finding. Node-local; never source.
/.head_build_check/

# `.probe/` — guard/serve reconnaissance scratch tree: probe .go spikes (guard_probe.go,
# serve_head.go, guard_*_recon.go) parked in a dot-dir so `go build`/`go test` skip them,
# plus overlay JSONs (overlay.json, ov_build.json, ov_test.json) from an `-overlay` probe.
# Node-local, regenerable, never source — the same class as /.tmp_overlay/ and
# /.head_build_check/ above.
/.probe/

# `.st_*` — per-session snapshot / overlay / commit-ladder scratch. A session that
# has to land on a churning shared trunk freezes a workspace to work against: an
# ad-hoc `.st_ladder.sh` builds `.st_full/` — a FULL mirror of the repo tree (its own
# .gitignore, AGENTS.md, internal/**, cmd/**, docs/**; ~180MB, 11k+ files) — regens a
# scorecard against that frozen copy in `.st_out/`/`.st_gen/`, and drives the commit
# through `fak commit`, dropping `.st_fc*.json` / `.st_ladder.log` / `.st_full_base`
# receipts and `.st_overlay*`/`.st_probe/`/`.st_pinned.txt` overlay state along the way.
# ALL of it is regenerable, node-local scratch — never source. Left unignored, `.st_full`
# alone dumps 11k+ entries into `git status` (burying real WIP), leaks into fak's durable
# `fak-wip` leaf checkpoints, AND — exactly like /.head_build_check/ above — makes every
# tree-walking governance gate scan a second mirrored copy of the whole repo and
# double-count. Root-anchored prefix so the whole ad-hoc family is caught by one rule and
# a tracked file that merely starts with "st" elsewhere is untouched.
/.st_*

# `.tmp-<issue>-head` / `.tmp-<n>-*` — a per-session HEAD-archive checkout (a `git archive
# HEAD | tar -x` copy of a package, e.g. `.tmp-3620-head/` holding cmd/fak) used to A/B a
# change against clean HEAD without touching the shared index. Regenerable, node-local
# scratch — the sibling of /.tmp/ and /.tmp_overlay/ above, just issue-suffixed.
/.tmp-*

# `.mcwitness/` — witness-cache reconnaissance scratch (a `main.go` spike parked in a
# dot-dir so `go build`/`go test` skip it). Regenerable, never source — same class as
# /.probe/ above.
/.mcwitness/

# `Microsoft/Windows/PowerShell/` — pwsh's ModuleAnalysisCache. A detached `pwsh` started
# without LOCALAPPDATA in its environment falls back to the working directory, so a
# background script launched from the clone root drops the cache here instead of under
# AppData. Machine-generated, never source, and it reads as a no-lane path in the
# `fak sync push` dirty-worktree report until it is ignored.
/Microsoft/
/.overlay4515

# --- root DOT namespace (denylist -> allowlist inversion) -------------------------
# The `/_*` block above inverted the '_'-prefix scratch convention. This does the same for
# the OTHER root scratch convention the fleet actually uses more: a DOT prefix. Sessions park
# overlay/probe/snapshot state in a dot-entry precisely BECAUSE Go and most tree-walkers skip
# dot-entries -- `.overlay3267/`, `.ovl5119neg/`, `.fak-overlay-5087/`, `.replay5120/`,
# `.sbom3279/` (a FULL second copy of the repo tree), `.parkprobecheck/`, `.tmp-3620-head/`,
# `.scratch-5254-*.json`, `.validate5087.json`, `.commitmsg-4334.txt`, `.dv5648.log`.
#
# Every one of those was named REACTIVELY, after it had already leaked -- and each session
# mints a fresh issue number, so the denylist can never catch up. `/.overlay4515` and
# `/.verify1259` above are two single-use rules that prove the treadmill: they ignore exactly
# one session's overlay and nothing else. So invert it. Ignore the root dot namespace by
# DEFAULT and re-include the legitimate entries, which are few and stable.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED ONLY -- the load-bearing safety property, exactly as with `/_*`. A gitignore
# `*` never matches `/`, so `/.*` matches ONLY root dot-entries: it can never reach
# `.github/workflows/*.yml`, `.claude/skills/**`, or a nested `internal/**/.keep` (witnessed
# with `git check-ignore` on each). The re-include list below is every root dot path
# `git ls-files` reports, with two deliberate deltas: `.dispatch-runs/` stays ignored (it
# already was, above -- operator-private telemetry that predates this block), and
# `.env.example` is listed though no such file exists yet, to preserve the `!.env.example`
# intent declared further up. Keep this list synchronized with the intentional tracked root
# dot paths so generated tool state remains private without hiding project configuration.
#
# To TRACK a new root dot path, add a `!` line here. Until you do, a bare `git add` will not
# sweep it in -- which is the point. Deliberate one-offs still work with `git add -f`.
#
# The consequence to know: `git clean -Xdf` (and `fak sweep`) will now reap these as the
# disposable scratch they are. Tree-walking gates mostly do NOT change behaviour here --
# branchrole's refaudit, for one, already pruned them via `ls-files --others` (no
# --exclude-standard), which drops ignored and untracked paths alike.
/.*
!/.aider.conf.yml
!/.agents
!/.claude
!/.claude-plugin
!/.codex
!/.continue
!/.dockerignore
!/.env.example
!/.gitattributes
!/.github
!/.gitignore
!/.gopls
!/.junie
!/.mcp.json

# Video-generation scratch output. Keep project JSON/tools, review proofs, and
# published final media committable; ignore only regenerable frame/output trees.
/tools/videogen/projects/*/out/
/tools/videogen/projects/*/frames/
/tools/videogen/projects/*/frames-hires/
/visuals/frames/

# Root-local captures from manual fleet/CLI diagnostics. These are regenerated JSON,
# stdout/stderr, help, process, and Go coverage dumps—not repository source. Keep the
# names root-anchored so legitimate fixtures with the same basename remain trackable.
/dosloop.out
/dosloop.err
/tick.json
/router.json
/fak_help.txt
/ps5.out
/ps5.err
/$cover

# Dot-prefixed session transaction captures (for example .st_<issue>_commit.log and
# .st_<issue>_precommit_hash.txt) are failed-command diagnostics, not package source.
# No tracked file uses this namespace; ignore it recursively where a session ran.
**/.st_*
/fak-orchestration-runs
/fak-orchestration-launches
/tools/bus/instances
